<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ site_title }} — {{ date }}</title>
{% include 'styles.html.j2' %}
</head>
<body>
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to report</a>
<div class="wrap">
<nav class="report-nav" aria-label="Report navigation"><a class="brand" href="./index.html">{{ site_title }}</a><div class="nav-links"><a href="#momentum">Climbers</a><a href="#discoveries">Fresh finds</a><a href="#categories">Categories</a><a class="notebook-link" href="#notebook">My notebook <span id="notebook-nav-count">0</span></a></div><span class="report-date">{{ country|upper }} · {{ date }}</span></nav>
<header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">Daily discovery brief</p><h1>Spot momentum.<br>Find your next idea.</h1><p class="intro muted">Discover rising apps. Save what stands out. Turn a signal into a small experiment.</p></header>
<main id="main">
<div class="stats"><div class="stat"><strong>{{ insights.total_apps }}</strong><span>unique apps tracked</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>{{ total_new }}</strong><span>newly observed apps</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>{{ insights.total_charts }}</strong><span>charts captured</span></div></div>
{% if insights.gap_days and insights.gap_days > 1 %}
<aside class="notice"><strong>Tracking resumed after {{ insights.gap_days }} days.</strong><p>The previous snapshot is from {{ insights.previous_date }}. “Newly observed” means new to our saved history; these apps may have entered during the gap. Momentum requires a snapshot on the exact comparison date.</p></aside>
{% elif insights.baseline %}
<aside class="notice"><strong>Your first baseline is ready.</strong><p>Future daily snapshots will reveal movement. Today’s apps establish the starting point and aren’t counted as new entrants.</p></aside>
{% endif %}
<section class="opportunity-filters" aria-labelledby="filters-heading">
<div class="section-top"><div><p class="eyebrow">Your research focus</p><h2 id="filters-heading">Focus your search</h2><p class="muted">Choose a market and find the apps worth a closer look.</p></div><button type="button" id="reset-filters">Reset filters</button></div>
<form id="opportunity-filters">
<div class="filter-grid">
<label>Category<select id="category"><option value="any">All categories</option>{% for genre, label in categories %}<option value="{{ genre }}">{{ label }}</option>{% endfor %}</select></label>
<label>Chart type<select id="chart-type"><option value="any">Free &amp; paid</option><option value="top-free">Free</option><option value="top-paid">Paid</option></select></label>
<label>Release age<select id="release-age"><option value="any">Any age</option><option value="90">Within 90 days</option><option value="180">Within 180 days</option><option value="365">Within 1 year</option></select></label>
</div><details id="advanced-filters" class="advanced-filters"><summary>Momentum filters <span id="advanced-count"></span></summary><div class="content"><div class="filter-grid advanced-grid"><label>Minimum rank gain<select id="min-gain"><option value="1">1+ places</option><option value="5">5+ places</option><option value="10">10+ places</option><option value="20">20+ places</option><option value="40">40+ places</option></select></label>
<label>Momentum<select id="momentum-mode"><option value="any">All rises · sustained first</option><option value="sustained">Sustained climbs only</option></select></label>
</div><label class="check-label"><input id="hide-games" type="checkbox"> Hide games across all charts</label><p class="research">Gain and momentum apply to climbers. Category, chart type, age, and hidden items also apply to fresh finds. Age filters exclude apps with unknown release dates.</p></div></details>
</form><div id="active-filters" class="active-filters" aria-label="Active filters"></div>
<details id="hidden-manager"><summary>Hidden apps &amp; developers (<span id="hidden-count">0</span>)</summary><div class="content"><p id="storage-status" class="muted">Stored on this browser only.</p><div id="hidden-items"></div><button id="restore-hidden" type="button">Restore all hidden items</button></div></details>
</section>
<section id="momentum" class="section" aria-labelledby="momentum-heading">
<div class="section-top"><div><p class="eyebrow">Momentum</p><h2 id="momentum-heading">Five climbers to investigate</h2><p class="muted">Your strongest matching signals, with sustained climbs first. Open the evidence to see what changed.</p></div><div class="control"><label for="window">Compare</label><select id="window">{% for w in insights.windows %}<option value="{{ w.days }}"{% if w.days == insights.default_window %} selected{% endif %}>{{ w.days }} day{% if w.days != 1 %}s{% endif %}</option>{% endfor %}</select></div></div>
<noscript><p>Enable JavaScript to use filters, hide apps, or switch windows. The unfiltered default comparison is shown below.</p></noscript>
<div aria-live="polite">
{% for w in insights.windows %}
<div data-window="{{ w.days }}"{% if w.days != insights.default_window %} hidden{% endif %}>
{% if not w.available %}
<div class="empty"><p class="eyebrow">Collecting history</p><h3>No {{ w.days }}-day comparison yet</h3><p>We don’t have a matching chart snapshot for {{ w.baseline_date }}. Keep capturing daily reports to unlock this window.</p><p class="muted">There is no measured momentum to rank today in this window. Explore the recent releases below while the baseline builds.</p></div>
{% else %}
<div data-filter-results="{{ w.days }}">
<p class="muted">{{ w.baseline_date }} → {{ date }} · {{ w.compared_charts }}/{{ insights.total_charts }} comparable charts · {{ w.matched_apps }} apps ranked on both dates · {{ w.total_movers }} unique climbers</p>
{% if not w.shortlist %}<div class="empty"><h3>No measured climbers in this window</h3><p>Apps present on both dates did not improve their rank in a comparable chart. A new chart appearance has no known starting rank.</p></div>{% endif %}
<div class="cards">
{% for app in w.shortlist %}
<article class="card"><div class="app">{% if app.artwork %}<img src="{{ app.artwork }}" alt="" loading="lazy">{% endif %}<div><h3><a href="{{ app.url }}">{{ app.name or app.id }}</a></h3><small>{{ app.artist }}</small></div></div>
<span class="badge">{{ app.signal.pattern }}</span><div class="gain">↑ {{ app.signal.gain }} places</div><p>{{ app.signal.label }}<br><strong>#{{ app.signal.previous }} → #{{ app.signal.rank }}</strong> in {{ w.days }} day{% if w.days != 1 %}s{% endif %}</p>
<svg class="spark" viewBox="0 0 200 65" role="img" aria-label="Observed rank history for {{ app.name }}. Lower ranks are better. Gaps represent missing observations.">
<line class="gridline" x1="5" y1="5" x2="195" y2="5"/><line class="gridline" x1="5" y1="60" x2="195" y2="60"/>
{% for point in app.signal.observations %}{% if point.rank is not none %}
{% set x = 5 + loop.index0 * 190 / w.days %}{% set y = 5 + (point.rank - 1) * 55 / 99 %}
{% if not loop.first %}{% set previous = app.signal.observations[loop.index0 - 1] %}{% if previous.rank is not none %}<line x1="{{ 5 + (loop.index0 - 1) * 190 / w.days }}" y1="{{ 5 + (previous.rank - 1) * 55 / 99 }}" x2="{{ x }}" y2="{{ y }}"/>{% endif %}{% endif %}<circle cx="{{ x }}" cy="{{ y }}" r="3"><title>{{ point.date }}: #{{ point.rank }}</title></circle>
{% endif %}{% endfor %}</svg>
<small>{{ app.signal.observed_days }}/{{ w.days + 1 }} daily observations · #1 at top</small>
<div class="metric">{% if app.signal.streak > 0 %}<span class="badge">{{ app.signal.streak }} consecutive daily gain{% if app.signal.streak != 1 %}s{% endif %}</span>{% endif %}<span class="badge">Rising in {{ app.rising_charts }} chart{% if app.rising_charts != 1 %}s{% endif %}</span><p>{% if app.age_days is not none %}Released {{ app.age_days }} days ago{% else %}Release date unavailable{% endif %} · First observed {{ app.first_seen }}</p></div>
<details><summary>Inspect the rank evidence</summary><ul>{% for point in app.signal.observations %}<li>{{ point.date }}: {% if point.rank is not none %}#{{ point.rank }}{% else %}No observation{% endif %}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></details>
<p class="research">Research next: read recent critical reviews and look for a repeated task users struggle to complete.</p>
</article>
{% endfor %}
</div>
{% if w.movers %}<div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>More climbers · one strongest chart per app</caption><thead><tr><th>App</th><th>Chart</th><th>Previous</th><th>Now</th><th>Gain</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for app in w.movers %}<tr><td><a href="{{ app.url }}">{{ app.name or app.id }}</a></td><td>{{ app.signal.label }}</td><td class="numeric">#{{ app.signal.previous }}</td><td class="numeric">#{{ app.signal.rank }}</td><td class="numeric">↑ {{ app.signal.gain }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>{% endif %}
</div>
{% endif %}
</div>
{% endfor %}
</div>
<p class="research">Rank movement is a research signal, not evidence of revenue, organic growth, or an unmet need. Apps missing from the earlier chart are not assigned an invented starting rank.</p>
</section>
<section id="discoveries" class="section" aria-labelledby="discovery-heading"><div class="section-top"><div><p class="eyebrow">Fresh discoveries</p><h2 id="discovery-heading">Fresh finds</h2><p class="muted">Recently released apps appearing in our history for the first time. A starting point for research.</p></div></div>
<p id="discovery-count" class="muted" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="cards" id="discovery-cards">{% for app in insights.discoveries %}<article class="card"><div class="app">{% if app.artwork %}<img src="{{ app.artwork }}" alt="" loading="lazy">{% endif %}<div><h3><a href="{{ app.url }}">{{ app.name or app.id }}</a></h3><small>{{ app.artist }}</small></div></div><span class="badge">Released {{ app.age_days }} days ago</span><p><strong>#{{ app.best_chart.rank }}</strong> in {{ app.best_chart.label }}</p><p class="muted">Appears in {{ app.charts|length }} tracked chart{% if app.charts|length != 1 %}s{% endif %}.</p><details><summary>All current chart positions</summary><ul>{% for chart in app.charts %}<li>#{{ chart.rank }} · {{ chart.label }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></details><p class="research">Research next: identify the core user problem and check whether reviews support demand for it.</p></article>{% else %}<div class="empty"><h3>No qualifying discoveries today</h3><p>Apps need a known release date within the last 180 days and must be new to saved history.</p></div>{% endfor %}</div>
</section>
<details id="notebook" class="section">
<summary class="notebook-heading"><span>My opportunity notebook<small>Your shortlist, ideas, and next experiments</small></span><span class="count-pill"><span id="notebook-count">0</span> saved</span></summary>
<div class="content">
<p class="muted">Keep promising apps here and develop your own angle. Chart positions update when you open a new report.</p>
<div class="actions"><button type="button" id="notebook-export">Export notebook</button><label class="import-label" for="notebook-import">Import notebook<input type="file" id="notebook-import" accept=".json,application/json"></label><button type="button" id="notebook-undo" hidden>Undo removal</button><button type="button" id="notebook-backup" hidden>Download unreadable backup</button></div>
<p class="research">Saved on this browser only. Export a backup to move your ideas to another device. Imports keep existing notes; filters and hidden apps are separate.</p>
<p id="notebook-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div id="notebook-entries"></div>
</div></details>
<section id="categories" class="section" aria-labelledby="categories-heading">
<p class="eyebrow">Explore the evidence</p><h2 id="categories-heading">Newly observed apps by category</h2>
<p class="muted">{{ total_new }} unique apps across all categories. An app can appear in several charts.</p>
<div class="category-toolbar">
<div class="category-controls">
<label class="category-search">Find a category<input id="category-search" type="search" placeholder="Try Productivity, Books, or Games" autocomplete="off" aria-controls="category-results"></label>
<label>Chart<select id="category-chart"><option value="all">Free &amp; paid</option><option value="top-free">Free</option><option value="top-paid">Paid</option></select></label>
<label>Sort by<select id="category-sort"><option value="new">Most new apps</option><option value="name">Category A–Z</option></select></label>
</div>
<div class="category-options"><label class="check-label"><input id="category-show-empty" type="checkbox"> Show empty charts</label><button id="category-reset" type="button">Reset category filters</button></div>
<div class="category-results-bar"><p id="category-results-count" class="muted" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="category-expand"><button type="button" id="category-expand">Expand results</button><button type="button" id="category-collapse">Collapse results</button></div></div>
</div>
<div id="category-empty" class="empty" hidden><h3>No categories match</h3><p>Try a shorter search, choose another chart type, or show empty charts.</p><button id="category-empty-reset" type="button">Show categories with new apps</button></div>
<div id="category-results">
{% for section in sections %}<details class="section-details" data-feed-type="{{ section.feed_type }}" data-category="{{ section.genre_label }}" data-new-count="{{ section.count }}"><summary><span class="category-title">{{ section.genre_label }}<small>{{ section.feed_label }}</small></span><span class="count-pill">{{ section.count }} new</span></summary><div class="content">{% if section.apps %}<div class="category-grid">{% for app in section.apps %}<div class="app">{% if app.artwork %}<img src="{{ app.artwork }}" alt="" loading="lazy">{% endif %}<div><a href="{{ app.url }}">{{ app.name }}</a><br><small>{{ app.artist }} · #{{ app.rank }}</small></div></div>{% endfor %}</div>{% else %}<p class="muted">No newly observed apps in this category.</p>{% endif %}<a class="category-back" href="#categories">Back to category search ↑</a></div></details>{% endfor %}
</div>
</section>
<details class="section"><summary>How we distinguish momentum from a jump</summary><div class="content"><p><strong>Sustained climb:</strong> rank improved on each of at least three consecutive days ending on the report date, within the selected comparison window.</p><p><strong>One-day rise:</strong> only one daily change is measured. <strong>Jump-led rise:</strong> no sustained streak and one daily gain accounts for at least 70% of the window’s net gain. <strong>Mixed movement:</strong> positive net gain spread over multiple days without a current three-day streak. <strong>Limited history:</strong> intermediate observations are missing and there is no qualifying current streak.</p><p>Missing days and missing chart positions break streaks. These labels describe observed ranks, not forecasts.</p></div></details></main><footer>Apple chart observations · {{ country|upper }} · Generated {{ now }}<br>Release age comes from Apple’s feed. First observed refers to this tracker’s history, not an app’s first-ever chart entry.</footer>
</div>
<script id="opportunity-data" type="application/json">{{ insights.filter_data | tojson }}</script>
<script>{% include 'notebook.js' %}</script>
<script>{% include 'opportunities.js' %}</script>
</body></html>
